WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.813
Step four turns on the telemetry, in
Bash, as a Security Administrator.

2
00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:09.656
The guide's command puts a diagnostic
setting named G S A network telemetry on

3
00:00:09.656 --> 00:00:14.500
the tenant, pointing at your test workspace,
with the four categories enabled.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.112
This is the lab's first write to
the tenant, and Module 6 removes it.

5
00:00:19.112 --> 00:00:21.713
The GET that follows
should list the setting,

6
00:00:21.713 --> 00:00:24.313
with the four categories
and your workspace.

7
00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:26.149
Step five checks freshness.

8
00:00:26.149 --> 00:00:31.088
In the workspace's Logs, run the guide's
union query across the four tables.

9
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:36.137
The guide's Validate is that each category
has rows within an hour of pilot traffic.

10
00:00:36.137 --> 00:00:40.263
There's no pilot traffic yet,
so expect few or no rows now.

11
00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:45.340
Run the query again after Module 2's
lab, and keep both results as evidence.
